      "content": "a \"quiet break\" doesn't really cut it though. it's not about a weekend off or a vacation. it's that deep, fundamental exhaustion where even breathing feels like a chore i didn't sign up for. i feel like i've been running a marathon for ten years and i can't even see the finish line. i just want a permanent kind of stillness. something that doesn't require me to wake up and do it all again tomorrow.",
